Inject NVIDIA Reflex latency markers
By default %PRODUCTNAME% injects NVIDIA Reflex latency markers into any Direct3D11 and Direct3D12 applications, which do not support NVIDIA Reflex technology natively. 
Latency markers integration allows you to monitor detailed per-stage timings and latencies on different stages of rendering pipeline. 
However, some applications (e.g. Workers And Resources: Soviet Republic or Overwatch 2) can be incompatible with latency markers injection, so you may use this option for troubleshooting to disable it either globally or for some specific applications.

Hints:
- This setting is specific to currently selected application profile.
- You may load Reflex.ovl overlay layout in OverlayEditor plugin to analyze NVIDIA Reflex latencies on different stages of rendering pipeline.
- You may disable user interface tooltips via <User interface> tab in advanced properties.
